<title>GREECE: Athens bourse/FTSE to set up new stock index.</title>
<headline>Athens bourse/FTSE to set up new stock index.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens Stock Exchange and FTSE International signed an agreement on Friday to introduce a new real-time index next year which will support derivative trading, a joint news release said.</p>
<p>The index will be designed by FTSE and will be calculated by the Athens Stock Exchange. It will include a basket of stocks, it said.</p>
<p>The index will group 20 to 25 companies, and represent about 60 to 70 percent of market capitalisation.</p>
<p>FTSE International is a private limited company owned by the Financial Times Ltd and the London Stock Exchange. It is best known for the FTSE 100, the main index for the London Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>--Steve Weeks, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
